FFT Verification Flow (radix-4)
================================


Please Run the commands in order:-

1.) python3 input_result_generator.py
2.) python3 generate_mcode.py              -> writes fft_N.mcode  (e.g. fft_64.mcode)
3.) ./run.sh fft_N                         (e.g. ./run.sh fft_64)
4.) python3 accuracy_out.py

Supported sizes: N = 16, 32, 64, ..., 2048 (powers of 2).  The simulator's data
memory holds 8192 64-bit words and the FFT needs 3N of them.

Alternative:-
Run this command:  ./run_fft_verification.sh	//this shell script runs all the commands in order

=====================
Explanation Below
=====================

1. Generate FFT Inputs and Golden Outputs

    python3 input_result_generator.py

This script generates:

    data.map    - Input samples and twiddle factors in float64 hex format.
    input.txt   - Input samples and twiddle factors in decimal format.
    result.txt  - Golden FFT outputs in float64 hex format (bit-reversed order).
    output.txt  - Golden FFT outputs in decimal format (bit-reversed order).

Input samples are randomly generated float64 values in the range:

    [-1000000.0, +1000000.0]

data.map format (one 64-bit float64 value = 16 hex digits per entry):

    0      : x[0].real
    1      : x[0].imag
    ...
    2N-1   : x[N-1].imag            inputs   : 2N entries (2N x 16 hex digits)

    2N     : W[0].real
    2N + 1 : W[0].imag
    ...
    3N - 1 : W[N/2 - 1].imag        twiddles : N entries (N/2 complex W_N^k, k < N/2)

Total entries in data.map: 3N   (3N * 8 bytes)

The FFT runs in place: it reads and writes only these 3N entries.  Only the
N/2 twiddles W_N^k (k < N/2) are stored; the radix-4 code obtains every other
twiddle it needs from them by symmetry (W^3k = conj(W[N-3k]) for 3k > N/2) and
re-uses the twiddle area for the smaller per-stage tables.


2. Generate FFT mcode

    python3 generate_mcode.py          (prompts for N)
    python3 generate_mcode.py 256      (or pass N on the command line)

This script reads the reference file fftN_new.mcode and
writes a new file

    fft_N.mcode          e.g. fft_64.mcode, fft_256.mcode, fft_1024.mcode

every time it is executed.

fftN_new.mcode is the radix-4 reference.  It is a complete, runnable N=64
program followed by a library of blocks needed by other sizes.  Each block is
delimited by "//@BLOCK name ... //@END" and every N-dependent immediate carries
a "//@ formula" annotation.  The generator selects/orders/repeats the blocks for
the requested N and evaluates the formulas; the instruction schedule itself is
taken unchanged from the reference.  See the header of fftN_new.mcode for the
algorithm and register map.


3. Run FFT Assembly Program

    ./run.sh fft_N

This assembles and runs the FFT implementation.

The program reads inputs from data.map, performs the FFT computation,
and compares the generated outputs against the golden outputs in
result.txt.

A log file named run.log is generated containing the comparison results.


4. Generate Accuracy Report

    python3 accuracy_out.py

This script parses run.log and generates:

    accuracy_report.txt

It also prints a summary on the terminal showing:

    - Max Relative Error (%)
    - Average Relative Error (%)
    - Max Absolute Error
    - Average Absolute Error
    - RMS Error
    - Data Memory used (2N input entries, N twiddle entries)
    - Bundles executed(Ticks), instructions per bundle(IPB) and efficiency

[IPB = non-null instructions / bundles executed; the machine maximum is 8]

accuracy_report.txt contains detailed per-sample accuracy information.
Results differ from numpy only in the last bits (rounding); the report shows
the size of these differences.


=====================
Implementation
=====================

In-place decimation-in-frequency radix-4 FFT (output in bit-reversed order,
same as before).  For odd log2(N) the last radix-4 stage (L=8) is fused with
the final radix-2 stage.

    stage 0 (L = N)     radix-4 butterfly pairs; W^k, W^2k, W^3k from the
                        N/2-entry table (W^3k by conjugate symmetry when 3k > N/2)
    stages L = N/4 ...  generic radix-4 stages, twiddles from a compacted table
    L = 16 / L = 8      constant twiddles folded into the butterflies
    L = 4               trivial butterflies

Every loop is software pipelined: one iteration of the main butterfly loop
processes two radix-4 butterflies (k, k+1) with 256-bit loads/stores in
11 bundles (81 instructions + branch).


==================================================================
Note: for a new run do ./clean.sh before following the aforementioned steps.
